# 3. Credit Calculation and Display Rules

The existing `creditService.ts` defines:

- Standard Scan: 1 credit per input minute.
- Deep Scan: 2 credits per input minute.
- Minimum billing duration: 1 minute.
- Partial minutes are rounded up using `Math.ceil(durationSeconds / 60)`.

Preserve this calculation.

The pricing interface must distinguish between:

**Credits** — the actual account balance and amount deducted by the system.

**Input Minutes** — the approximate video duration that can be inspected with a particular scan mode.

Never label credits as minutes without explaining the conversion.

Display the following comparison clearly:

| Plan | Credits | Standard Scan | Deep Scan |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Free | 10 | 10 min | 5 min |
| Creator | 30 | 30 min | 15 min |
| Pro | 75 | 75 min | 37 min + 1 credit remaining |
| Agency / MCN | 600 | 600 min | 300 min |
| Audit Once | 60 | 60 min | 30 min |

Add a concise explanation:

"Standard Scan uses 1 credit per input minute. Deep Scan uses 2 credits per input minute. Partial input minutes are rounded up to the next whole minute."

Make the distinction visible on desktop and mobile.

Do not alter server-side credit calculations to accommodate frontend display requirements.

